<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (GPT-5.6 Sol)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol-medium>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol-medium> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol";
    dc:identifier "gpt-5.6-sol-medium".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch08-07--gpt> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch08-07: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.67";
    dc:description "Scale-specific perturbation growth is well defined and can be tested computationally in public flow fields. Existing databases cover important but narrow canonical geometries and do not represent almost all real and model flows. Controlled perturbation ensembles may also require new simulations rather than analysis alone.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/mixed";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: For ensembles of nearly identical initial flow fields, track divergence of low-wavenumber velocity and pressure observables while varying viscosity and flow regime. The claim predicts decay or negligible growth of large-scale differences in almost all sampled flows, including turbulent cases.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Almost all cases lacks a sampling distribution over flows.", "Large scale and discernible require chosen filters and tolerances.", "Single trajectories do not provide controlled pairs of nearby initial conditions.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.83"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch08-07--gpt--dataset-1>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.666"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch08-07--gpt--dataset-1> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/EvidenceItem>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Candidate dataset: Johns Hopkins Turbulence Databases";
    dc:description "public high-resolution turbulent flow fields for perturbation and scale-dependent divergence analyses";
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://turbulence.pha.jhu.edu/>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch08-07--gpt--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
